desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Ocamllint Marshal"
	title_zh: "Ocamllint Marshal"
	type: vuln
	level: middle
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-ocamllint-marshal"
	risk: "Security"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `ocamllint-marshal` (ocaml/lang/security/marshal.yaml).
Original message: Marshaling is currently not type-safe and can lead to insecure behaviour when untrusted data is marshalled. Marshalling can lead to out-of-bound reads as well.
CWE: CWE-502: Deserialization of Untrusted Data
References:
- https://eternal.red/2021/secure-ocaml-sandbox/
Note: source-mode regex approximation of a safe-literal Semgrep pattern.
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review this occurrence and replace it with a safer alternative.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.ml": <<<POS
input_value
POS
	"safefile://pos.ml": <<<NEG
Printf.printf
NEG
)

${*.ml}.pattern_regex(/(?:input_value)|(?:Marshal\.from_channel)|(?:Marshal\.from_bytes)|(?:Marshal\.from_string)/) as $p0
${*.mli}.pattern_regex(/(?:input_value)|(?:Marshal\.from_channel)|(?:Marshal\.from_bytes)|(?:Marshal\.from_string)/) as $p1
$p0 + $p1 as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Ocamllint Marshal",
	title_zh: "Ocamllint Marshal",
	message: "Ocamllint Marshal detected.",
}
